== successor (k = 1) ==
2q/(a(1-q^2)^2) * (q - q_n) with q = 3/4, a = 6, q - q_n = (3/4) 3^-n:  coefficient of 3^-n = 48/49  (the note: 48/49)
eps(n) <= (48/49) 3^-n for n < 400: True
6^5 eps(n) <= 2^(13 - 1.58 n) for all n <= 2000 (exact): True
   and for all n by the closed form: log2(6^5 * 48/49) = 12.895065 <= 13 and log2 3 = 1.5849625 >= 1.58
the first report's 6^5 eps(n) <= 2^(12.9 - 1.585 n): fails first at n = 132, and at every n from there to 400: True
   (reason: 1.585 > log2 3 = 1.5849625; the margin 12.9 - 12.895065 = 0.004935 is used up at n = 131.6)
   a correct pair of rounded constants: 6^5 eps(n) <= 2^(12.9 - 1.5849 n) for all n: True (checked to 400; 1.5849 < log2 3)

== addition (k = 2) ==
q = 3 - sqrt 5 = 0.763932023;  2q/(a(1-q^2)^2) = 1.258777;  times 2 (5/7)^2 = 1.284466  (the note: 1.2845)
partial sums P_N of T_s/5^s: P_N <= 4/5 + P_(N-1)/5 + P_(N-1)^2/5 and P_N < 2 for N < 400: True   (P_399 = 1.91080)
q - q_m <= 2 (5/7)^(m+1) for m <= 3000: True
eps(n+1) <= 1.2845 (5/7)^n for n <= 3000: True
7^13 * 1.2845 * (5/7)^n <= 2^(36.5 - 0.485 n) holds from n = 836 on (exact; the note: 836); at n = 835 it fails: True
7^13 eps(n+1) <= 2^(36.5 - 0.485 n) for all n <= 3000 (high precision): True

== where the bounds say something ==
7^13 eps(m) < 1 first at m = 60  (Corollary 4: m = n + 1, so n = 59)
Proposition 4a(2) gives 7^13 eps(m) with n >= m^2 (h + 1): below 1 only for m >= 60, that is n >= 3600 (h + 1):
   h = 1: n >= 7200;   at n = 200 it allows m <= 10 and the bound is 2^27.5  (Corollary 4 without missing pairs: 2^-71.1)
   h = 2: n >= 10800;   at n = 200 it allows m <= 8 and the bound is 2^28.8  (Corollary 4 without missing pairs: 2^-71.1)
   h = 5: n >= 21600;   at n = 200 it allows m <= 5 and the bound is 2^30.9  (Corollary 4 without missing pairs: 2^-71.1)
   n = 10000, h = 1: m = 70, bound 2^-5.3   (Corollary 4 without missing pairs: about 2^-4814)
   n = 10000, h = 3: m = 50, bound 2^5.1   (Corollary 4 without missing pairs: about 2^-4814)
   n = 40000, h = 1: m = 141, bound 2^-41.2   (Corollary 4 without missing pairs: about 2^-19364)
   n = 40000, h = 3: m = 100, bound 2^-20.6   (Corollary 4 without missing pairs: about 2^-19364)

== after Proposition 10: doubling ==
lower bound on a wrong belief at n = 2^j: 6^-(1.5 j^2 + 8.5 j + 8); upper bound from Theorem 2: 6^11 eps(m), largest m with 2^(m-2) + 1 <= n, i.e. m = j + 1
   j =  5: pinning between    -18.9 and    227.5 bits;   the note's 1.58 j - 28 =   -20.1,  3.9 j^2 + 22 j + 21 =    228.5
   j = 10: pinning between    -11.0 and    628.1 bits;   the note's 1.58 j - 28 =   -12.2,  3.9 j^2 + 22 j + 21 =    631.0
   j = 20: pinning between      4.9 and   2011.1 bits;   the note's 1.58 j - 28 =     3.6,  3.9 j^2 + 22 j + 21 =   2021.0
   j = 30: pinning between     20.7 and   4169.5 bits;   the note's 1.58 j - 28 =    19.4,  3.9 j^2 + 22 j + 21 =   4191.0
   j = 40: pinning between     36.6 and   7103.5 bits;   the note's 1.58 j - 28 =    35.2,  3.9 j^2 + 22 j + 21 =   7141.0
   exact constants: lower end = 1.5850 (j + 1) - 28.40 (from (48/49) 3^-m);  upper end = 3.877 j^2 + 21.97 j + 20.68
